# [[.Name]] plugin for CLIProxyAPI

Native [CLIProxyAPI](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI) (CPA) plugin that adds [[.Name]] as a provider, built on [cpa-provider-kit](https://[[.KitModule]]).

- **Sign-in:** paste an API key in a browser page served by CPA[[if .KeyURL]] (create one at <[[.KeyURL]]>)[[end]]. Several keys are load-balanced.
- **Models:** [[range $i, $m := .Models]][[if $i]], [[end]]`[[$m]]`[[end]], plus any listed in the `extra-models` setting.
- **Requests:** passed through untranslated to [[.Name]]'s native endpoints[[if .ChatPath]], Chat Completions `[[.ChatPath]]`[[end]][[if .AnthropicPath]], Anthropic Messages `[[.AnthropicPath]]`[[end]][[if .ResponsesPath]], Responses `[[.ResponsesPath]]`[[end]]. CPA translates other client protocols.

## Requirements

- CPA v8.0.47 or newer, running natively for its machine. Use the `aarch64` EasyCLIProxyAPI build on Apple Silicon; the Intel build runs under Rosetta and crashes when it loads Go plugins.

## Build and install

```bash
make test
make build      # dist/<goos>/<goarch>/[[.ID]].<ext>
make install    # copies into EasyCLIProxyAPI's plugins dir (override PLUGINS_DIR)
```

Or install `dist/<goos>/<goarch>/[[.ID]].<ext>` from EasyCLIProxyAPI's Plugins page. Then enable the plugin there or in `config.yaml`:

```yaml
plugins:
  enabled: true
  configs:
    [[.ID]]:
      enabled: true
      # base-url: [[.BaseURL]]
      # extra-models: []
```

Keep the library named `[[.ID]].<ext>` (or `[[.ID]]-v<version>.<ext>`); CPA derives the plugin ID from the file name.

## Add a key

Start the sign-in for `[[.ID]]` in EasyCLIProxyAPI (or `GET /v8/management/oauth/auth-url?provider=[[.ID]]`) and paste the key in the page that opens. For a remote CPA, upload an auth file instead:

```json
{ "type": "[[.ID]]", "api_key": "<key>", "label": "optional" }
```

## Release

Push a `v<version>` tag. `.github/workflows/release.yml` tests, builds Linux, macOS, and Windows libraries, and publishes `[[.ID]]_<version>_<goos>_<goarch>.zip` plus `checksums.txt` — the layout CPA's plugin store installs from.[[if .KitReplace]] Before the first release, publish cpa-provider-kit and remove the `replace` line from `go.mod`; CI cannot see the local checkout.[[end]]
